('9a5d75c2-ed08-54d2-afb7-302d753f2e46'::uuid,'28d81dcf-4bf7-51ee-8a3f-ed571ec8d617'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-D. EOC PERSONNEL DESIGNATION REGISTER\n\n| **EOC role**             | **Participating office** | **Primary personnel** | **Alternate** | **Relevant training / competence** | **Designation date** | **Availability / notes** |\n|--------------------------|--------------------------|-----------------------|---------------|------------------------------------|----------------------|--------------------------|\n| EOC Manager              |                          |                       |               |                                    |                      |                          |\n| Operations               |                          |                       |               |                                    |                      |                          |\n| Planning / Information   |                          |                       |               |                                    |                      |                          |\n| Logistics                |                          |                       |               |                                    |                      |                          |\n| Administration / Finance |                          |                       |               |                                    |                      |                          |\n| Agency / cluster liaison |                          |                       |               |                                    |                      |                          |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-D.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('a6a635cc-852a-55bd-8708-5ebcc93cc3bf'::uuid,'4c27e9a2-75d0-5ab4-8d30-de80e669aab0'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-E. DUTY HANDOVER CHECKLIST\n\n- Current hazard bulletins, warnings and validity periods.\n\n- Active incidents, affected locations and current operational status.\n\n- Pending decisions, approvals, requests and deadlines.\n\n- Resource requests, deployment status and unresolved constraints.\n\n- Communications, ICT, facility and equipment status.\n\n- Personnel availability, welfare concerns and relief arrangements.\n\n- Records, logs, reports and attachments completed or pending.\n\n- Escalation items and person / office responsible for follow-up.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-E.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('38cb4591-f60c-55c6-b7d0-3c9250561cc4'::uuid,'8f35192b-ad03-56b9-904a-60cb2594d593'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-F. LEGAL AND TECHNICAL VALIDATION REGISTER\n\n| **Validation issue**                                      | **Required reviewer**               | **Validation required before approval**                                                             |\n|-----------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Current legal establishment and approved CDRRMO structure | City Legal Office; HRMO; CDRRMO     | Identify existing ordinance/EO, approved organogram and any required amendatory issuance.           |\n| JMC No. 2014-1 requirements and current applicability     | HRMO; CDRRMO; OCD Region VIII       | Verify exact staffing, division and qualification requirements and any superseding guidance.        |\n| Plantilla, position classification and funding            | HRMO; Budget; DBM as applicable     | Confirm authorized items, salary grades, filled/vacant status and personnel-services affordability. |\n| Qualification standards and appointment status            | HRMO; CSC as applicable             | Verify current qualification standards and appointment records.                                     |\n| EOC staffing guidance and B4 requirements                 | OCD Region VIII; CDRRMO             | Confirm current EOC guidelines, role structure, alternates and liaison requirements.                |\n| 24/7 duty and compensation arrangements                   | HRMO; Budget; CLO                   | Verify duty, overtime, rest, hazard pay and other entitlements under applicable rules.              |\n| Insurance, PPE and psychosocial support                   | HRMO; CHO; OSH focal office; Budget | Verify available coverage, policy, funding, referral and incident-reporting procedures.             |\n| Privacy and personnel records                             | DPO; HRMO; Records Officer; ICT     | Confirm lawful basis, access, retention, security and disclosure controls.                          |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-F.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('42fbe119-3192-52a2-817f-505e85d935a7'::uuid,'85e5170e-7cb8-57d6-95c2-bd35b6f46fe5'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-G \\| SOP HR-01 – ANNUAL WORKFORCE PLANNING AND PLANTILLA REVIEW\n\n**Purpose**: Ensure the CDRRMO has a lawful, risk-informed and adequately planned workforce without creating unauthorized posts or commitments.\n\n**Trigger**: Annual planning cycle; material change in mandate, workload, risk profile, staffing or assessment results.\n\n**Owner**: CDRRMO Head jointly with HRMO for workforce-planning controls.\n\n**Procedure:**\n\n1\\. Division leads submit workload, service demand, outputs, critical functions and staffing availability.\n\n2\\. CDRRMO consolidates workload against LDRRMP priorities, statutory functions, operating hours and continuity requirements.\n\n3\\. HRMO certifies approved structure, plantilla, filled/vacant items, qualification standards and personnel status.\n\n4\\. Identify gaps by category: authorized vacancy, skills gap, workload imbalance, process inefficiency, equipment constraint or inter-office dependency.\n\n5\\. Develop options: internal redeployment within authority, training, process redesign, lawful temporary augmentation, or formal position/structure proposal.\n\n6\\. Budget assesses affordability and recurring costs; CLO reviews legal route; other offices review relevant impacts.\n\n7\\. Submit proposals to the competent approving authority. Do not implement unapproved structural or fiscal changes.\n\n8\\. Record approved actions, owners, deadlines and evidence; review quarterly and annually.\n\nRecords: annual workforce plan; certified plantilla; gap matrix; workload analysis; endorsements; approval; implementation and CAPA register.\n\nEscalation: unresolved critical vacancies or unsafe coverage are elevated to the Mayor through established administrative channels, with interim risk controls documented.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-G.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('8322bd13-4168-5416-8b83-efa12467cd91'::uuid,'0c47ee75-7e9d-5306-9fb1-3a56ad06e956'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-H \\| SOP HR-02 – POSITION DESCRIPTION AND COMPETENCY PROFILE CONTROL\n\n**Purpose**: Keep every authorized position''s duties, outputs, authority boundaries and competency requirements current and aligned with statutory CDRRMO functions.\n\n**Owner**: HRMO for official position-description control; CDRRMO Head for technical content.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. Identify new, revised or materially changed function.\n\n2\\. Division lead drafts role purpose, outputs, duties, reporting line, decision limits, interfaces, working conditions and competency profile.\n\n3\\. CDRRMO Head verifies alignment with RA 10121 and approved functional architecture.\n\n4\\. HRMO checks consistency with qualification standards, position classification and CSC requirements.\n\n5\\. CLO reviews legal implications where authority or delegation is affected.\n\n6\\. Obtain required approval; assign version and effective date.\n\n7\\. Communicate role and performance expectations to incumbent and supervisor.\n\n8\\. Review annually and after organizational, legal or operational change.\n\nRecords: approved PDF, competency profile, consultation record, approval and revision history.\n\nControl: a job description cannot expand statutory authority or substitute for a valid delegation.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-H.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('a4be90ec-234e-5701-87b0-b268dc16b432'::uuid,'844f110f-9691-5b15-ae90-e8d3a8a71bff'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-I \\| SOP HR-03 – RECRUITMENT, APPOINTMENT INTERFACE AND ONBOARDING\n\n**Purpose**: Ensure staffing actions are based on authorized positions and comply with civil-service and City HR rules.\n\n**Owner**: HRMO; CDRRMO provides technical role requirements and induction.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. HRMO confirms an authorized vacant plantilla item and applicable qualification standards.\n\n2\\. CDRRMO validates technical competencies and operational requirements without adding unauthorized eligibility criteria.\n\n3\\. HRMO processes publication, assessment, selection and documentation under the approved Merit Selection Plan and applicable CSC rules.\n\n4\\. Selection/recommendation is documented; appointing authority exercises appointment power.\n\n5\\. HRMO completes appointment, assumption and personnel-record requirements.\n\n6\\. CDRRMO supervisor conducts induction on mandate, MOO, role boundaries, safety, information security, privacy, records and coordination protocols.\n\n7\\. Agree initial outputs, supervision and learning needs; record completion.\n\n8\\. Review onboarding effectiveness and update induction materials.\n\nRecords: vacancy certification; approved PDF/QS; recruitment records; appointment; assumption; induction checklist; initial performance plan.\n\nControl: CDRRMO may not promise appointment, bypass HRMO or deploy an appointee before lawful assumption and required clearances.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-I.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('a42b6d32-1b96-5ad9-b938-ba416203e64d'::uuid,'dafc267f-f2be-51fb-99e4-c3590777ffea'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-J \\| SOP HR-04 – COMPETENCY ASSESSMENT AND LEARNING & DEVELOPMENT\n\n**Purpose**: Build demonstrable capability for risk reduction, preparedness, coordination and safe performance.\n\n**Owner**: CDRRMO Head; HRMO validates agency L&D and competency-based HR alignment.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. Extract competencies from approved position profiles and operational task requirements.\n\n2\\. Assess current capability using records, structured assessment, observed performance, exercises and supervisor validation.\n\n3\\. Identify proficiency gaps and prioritize by life-safety, legal compliance, criticality and likelihood of deployment.\n\n4\\. Prepare an annual L&D plan with objectives, target participants, prerequisites, provider, budget, schedule and evaluation method.\n\n5\\. Obtain HRMO and budget review and required approvals.\n\n6\\. Deliver training, coaching, mentoring, drills or supervised practice.\n\n7\\. Evaluate learning and demonstrated competence; attendance or certificates alone are insufficient for high-risk task authorization.\n\n8\\. Update competency records and duty eligibility; schedule refresher or remediation.\n\n9\\. Review outcomes and revise the plan using exercise and incident lessons.\n\nRecords: competency matrix; TNA; approved L&D plan; attendance; assessment; certificates; exercise evaluation; authorization/qualification register.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-J.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('a0de96e3-9c65-5d6c-85ef-0010eb9c4805'::uuid,'bd06e310-098b-5af3-91db-49f19c207902'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-K \\| SOP HR-05 – DUTY ROSTER, SHIFT HANDOVER AND PERSONNEL AVAILABILITY\n\n**Purpose**: Maintain reliable personnel coverage and safe transfer of responsibility during normal operations and heightened readiness.\n\n**Owner**: CDRRMO Head; division leads prepare and supervise rosters.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. Determine required coverage from approved service hours, hazard season, duty requirements and continuity plan.\n\n2\\. Confirm personnel availability, qualifications, alternates, leave, rest periods and constraints.\n\n3\\. Prepare roster and submit for approval under delegated authority.\n\n4\\. Publish roster securely and notify assigned personnel.\n\n5\\. Outgoing officers brief incoming officer on open tasks, warnings, incidents, contacts, equipment status, pending approvals and risks.\n\n6\\. Both officers acknowledge handover; record time, unresolved issues and escalation.\n\n7\\. Immediately report absence, unfilled post, unsafe fatigue or inability to cover a critical function to the supervisor.\n\n8\\. Arrange authorized replacement and record changes.\n\n9\\. Reconcile actual coverage, attendance and exceptions monthly; feed gaps to CAPA.\n\nRecords: duty roster; acknowledgement; attendance; handover checklist; exception and fatigue log.\n\nBoundary: this SOP does not define EOC activation level, incident command or operational period; refer to the designated EOC/ICS chapters.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-K.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('eb3df260-29a4-53dd-8bb4-07c67303e847'::uuid,'0ce9bff4-b53d-55fc-b926-932384187d3f'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-L \\| SOP HR-06 – EOC PERSONNEL DESIGNATION AND SURGE AUGMENTATION\n\n**Purpose**: Ensure personnel assigned to EOC functions are designated, available, competent and supported by their parent offices.\n\n**Owner**: CDRRMO Head for roster readiness; EOC Manager for activated EOC staffing coordination; HRMO for personnel administration.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. Identify EOC functions and minimum competencies from the approved EOC structure and job action sheets in the relevant chapters.\n\n2\\. Request nominations from City offices and partner agencies, including primary and alternate personnel.\n\n3\\. Verify role fit, training, contactability, availability, supervisor concurrence and conflict/continuity implications.\n\n4\\. Compile a controlled designation register; obtain approval by the authority specified in the EOC issuance.\n\n5\\. Conduct orientation and exercises; record gaps and refresher needs.\n\n6\\. On activation, EOC Manager requests staffing through approved activation procedures; parent offices release or substitute personnel consistent with authority and service continuity.\n\n7\\. Track attendance, shift rotation, welfare, access permissions and return-to-office arrangements.\n\n8\\. Deactivate or revise assignments through authorized procedures; reconcile records and lessons.\n\nRecords: designation instrument; roster; alternates; competency evidence; exercise records; release/return log.\n\nControl: designation to an EOC position does not transfer the person''s statutory agency mandate or create field command authority.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-L.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('9722d1b3-3f7e-5e29-afd4-45ab97cc558a'::uuid,'bda079cf-0360-5c94-b2ef-f65c245f062b'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-M \\| SOP HR-07 – PERSONNEL SAFETY, WELFARE, INJURY AND PSYCHOSOCIAL REFERRAL\n\n**Purpose**: Prevent harm and ensure prompt support for CDRRMO personnel and responders under the City''s responsibility.\n\n**Owner**: CDRRMO Head for implementation; HRMO, designated OSH personnel and health/MHPSS providers for their respective professional mandates.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. Identify task hazards and required controls before assignment; verify PPE, training, fitness and supervision.\n\n2\\. Brief personnel on hazards, stop-work authority, communications, emergency contacts and welfare arrangements.\n\n3\\. Monitor exposure, fatigue, hydration, rest, heat, psychosocial stress and changing conditions.\n\n4\\. If injury, exposure, unsafe condition or distress occurs, prioritize immediate safety, medical care and protective action.\n\n5\\. Notify supervisor and designated safety focal; complete incident report as soon as practicable without delaying care.\n\n6\\. Refer to appropriate medical, occupational health, insurance, HR or psychosocial service with consent and confidentiality safeguards.\n\n7\\. Assess return-to-duty, accommodation and restrictions through competent professionals and HRMO processes.\n\n8\\. Review causes and contributing system factors; implement corrective actions and verify effectiveness.\n\nRecords: task risk assessment; PPE issue register; briefing; incident/near-miss report; referral record with restricted access; corrective action and return-to-duty clearance.\n\nSafeguards: protect sensitive personal information; do not disclose diagnosis or counselling details in operational logs; comply with applicable OSH, privacy and mental health requirements.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-M.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('fc1052f3-2651-5b90-ad1c-b4e2f9c07c6b'::uuid,'a1781689-7c69-5c11-b6d1-f99201d66c85'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-N \\| SOP HR-08 – PERFORMANCE MANAGEMENT, RECORDS AND CORRECTIVE ACTION\n\n**Purpose**: Align individual performance with CDRRMO outputs and use evidence to improve capability and institutional processes.\n\n**Owner**: CDRRMO Head and supervisors for operational performance; HRMO for official SPMS and personnel record administration.\n\n**Procedure**:\n\n1\\. Cascade approved office targets into individual outputs consistent with official SPMS.\n\n2\\. Agree measurable deliverables, indicators, timelines and evidence with each staff member.\n\n3\\. Conduct periodic coaching and retain appropriate work evidence.\n\n4\\. Assess results fairly against approved standards and consider workload, resources, dependencies and system constraints.\n\n5\\. Identify whether the gap is individual, supervisory, procedural, resource-related or inter-agency.\n\n6\\. Agree support and corrective action; refer possible misconduct or administrative matters through HRMO and due process.\n\n7\\. Verify completion and effectiveness; recognize good performance under approved policies.\n\n8\\. Aggregate systemic issues for workforce planning, risk management and MOO revision.\n\nRecords: approved performance commitments; coaching records; evidence; improvement plan; CAPA; review and acknowledgement.\n\nControl: this SOP does not create a separate disciplinary process or override CSC rules, due process or the City''s SPMS.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-N.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('8cd803c0-7c3d-54ec-85da-0cf84f643044'::uuid,'9cd3b25d-8b71-5b03-8180-37534b5a11e3'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-O \\| WORKFORCE AND PLANTILLA REVIEW FORM (HR-F01)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                    | Required entry |\n|----------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Planning year / review date                              |                |\n| Division / functional area                               |                |\n| Approved organizational unit / issuance                  |                |\n| Authorized plantilla item / position title / item number |                |\n| Authorized / filled / vacant / acting / temporary status |                |\n| Required qualification standard and competency profile   |                |\n| Current workload, outputs and service coverage           |                |\n| Vacancy / capability / workload / continuity risk        |                |\n| Evidence reference and verification date                 |                |\n| Options assessed and rationale                           |                |\n| HRMO review / certification                              |                |\n| Budget review and recurring cost estimate                |                |\n| CLO review where required                                |                |\n| Approving authority / decision / date                    |                |\n| Action owner / due date / closure evidence               |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-O.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('0bb86123-0a8f-55f6-9937-5f952c5da34f'::uuid,'a4cfafbe-4b4c-5421-8684-628260e3bcc9'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-P \\| POSITION DESCRIPTION AND COMPETENCY PROFILE TEMPLATE (HR-F02)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                         | Required entry |\n|---------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Position title / item number / salary grade (as authorized)   |                |\n| Office / division / immediate supervisor                      |                |\n| Position purpose and contribution to RA 10121 functions       |                |\n| Major duties and measurable outputs                           |                |\n| Decision authority and limits / delegated authority reference |                |\n| Internal and external interfaces                              |                |\n| Minimum qualification standards verified by HRMO              |                |\n| Core, leadership and technical competencies                   |                |\n| Proficiency level and observable behavioural indicators       |                |\n| Work environment / hazards / PPE / duty requirements          |                |\n| Performance indicators and evidence sources                   |                |\n| Prepared by / reviewed by HRMO / approved by authority        |                |\n| Version / effective date / review date                        |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-P.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('593e5e0a-b23b-5d70-bb75-4e5f80d67069'::uuid,'bd2bda56-0e37-5910-ba8d-2107a7590b33'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-Q \\| TRAINING NEEDS AND COMPETENCY ASSESSMENT (HR-F03)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                       | Required entry |\n|-------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Position / incumbent / assessor / assessment date           |                |\n| Competency / task / proficiency required                    |                |\n| Current proficiency and evidence                            |                |\n| Gap and operational risk if unaddressed                     |                |\n| Priority / criticality                                      |                |\n| Learning intervention / prerequisite                        |                |\n| Provider / schedule / estimated cost                        |                |\n| Assessment method (test, observation, exercise, simulation) |                |\n| Demonstrated competence / authorization decision            |                |\n| Refresher due date / reassessment result                    |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-Q.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('df243a74-e48b-5b35-9d39-b4f7b7f23ca2'::uuid,'3fb35d44-6b35-5977-80d1-49a0037adc37'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-R \\| DUTY ROSTER AND HANDOVER FORM (HR-F04)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                                | Required entry |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Duty period / shift / function                                       |                |\n| Primary officer / alternate / contact                                |                |\n| Required competency and qualification verified                       |                |\n| Supervisor approval / date                                           |                |\n| Outgoing officer: open tasks, warnings, incidents, pending decisions |                |\n| Equipment / communications / access status                           |                |\n| Incoming officer acknowledgement / time                              |                |\n| Unresolved risk / escalation / assigned owner                        |                |\n| Fatigue / rest / welfare concern and action                          |                |\n| Exception / replacement / approval reference                         |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-R.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('0d107f75-b92c-5f70-9736-0a5b7189eb99'::uuid,'51870f29-6811-5c03-8d0b-1df106573bc8'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-S \\| EOC PERSONNEL DESIGNATION REGISTER (HR-F05)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                | Required entry |\n|------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| EOC function / position / job action sheet reference |                |\n| Parent office / agency                               |                |\n| Primary nominee / alternate                          |                |\n| Supervisor concurrence / designation authority       |                |\n| Relevant training / competency evidence              |                |\n| Contact and availability verification date           |                |\n| Access / information classification requirements     |                |\n| Exercise participation / performance observations    |                |\n| Activation attendance / shift history                |                |\n| Release / return-to-duty / review date               |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-S.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('be199b4c-5413-581a-a1c7-e03bdd880f33'::uuid,'957e7bed-18fa-529e-b5d8-e38b08b21f65'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-T \\| PERSONNEL SAFETY, INJURY AND WELFARE REPORT (HR-F06)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                                      | Required entry |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Incident / near-miss reference; date/time/location                         |                |\n| Task / activity / supervisor                                               |                |\n| Hazard / exposure / event description (factual)                            |                |\n| Immediate protective action and medical assistance                         |                |\n| PPE / training / briefing / supervision status                             |                |\n| Persons notified and time                                                  |                |\n| Referral made (restricted details stored separately)                       |                |\n| Work restriction / accommodation / fitness decision by competent authority |                |\n| Root/contributing factors and corrective action                            |                |\n| Verification / effectiveness / closure date                                |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-T.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('056851be-bfeb-54bc-814a-3f08aa62fd1d'::uuid,'b6874943-8b79-5a4f-b897-36d98f054ea6'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-U \\| CHAPTER 2 CAPA AND QUALITY REVIEW REGISTER (HR-F07)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                         | Required entry |\n|---------------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Finding source / indicator reference (e.g., A2.1–A2.7)        |                |\n| Nonconformity / gap and evidence                              |                |\n| Risk / consequence / priority                                 |                |\n| Root cause (system, process, competency, resource, interface) |                |\n| Corrective action / expected result                           |                |\n| Accountable owner / responsible actors                        |                |\n| Resources / approval dependency / due date                    |                |\n| Implementation evidence                                       |                |\n| Effectiveness test / verifier / review date                   |                |\n| Status / escalation / closure authorization                   |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-U.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('56c71f18-974c-5cbb-8dc0-d595c36f9c1f'::uuid,'8016a091-d567-5dcd-89a2-19624f79f243'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-V \\| CHAPTER 2 RECORDS AND CONTROLLED DOCUMENT REGISTER (HR-F08)\n\n**Purpose**: Standardized record for the process identified in the title. Complete only fields necessary for the function; maintain restricted personal or sensitive information separately with access controls.\n\n| Field                                                   | Required entry |\n|---------------------------------------------------------|----------------|\n| Record / document title and code                        |                |\n| Owner / custodian / system of record                    |                |\n| Version / approval / effective date                     |                |\n| Classification / personal data category                 |                |\n| Authorized access / sharing basis                       |                |\n| Retention and disposition authority                     |                |\n| Backup / security / recovery control                    |                |\n| Review date / superseded version / disposition evidence |                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-V.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft'),
('d6a1d908-9e65-51d2-995b-177b4159c507'::uuid,'01d89334-45a7-5217-86f7-e28f30184ca1'::uuid,'v0.1 assessment-informed draft',E'# ANNEX 2-W \\| CHAPTER 2 SOP AND FORM CROSS-REFERENCE REGISTER\n\n| SOP   | Primary forms / records                          | Related section          | Process owner                |\n|-------|--------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|\n| HR-01 | HR-F01; workforce plan; certified plantilla      | 2.8; 2.18; 2.21.1–2.21.2 | CDRRMO Head / HRMO           |\n| HR-02 | HR-F02; PDF and competency register              | 2.7; 2.9; 2.21.2         | HRMO / CDRRMO Head           |\n| HR-03 | HR-F02; recruitment and onboarding records       | 2.9; 2.14; 2.21.3        | HRMO                         |\n| HR-04 | HR-F03; TNA; L&D plan; competency register       | 2.12; 2.21.4             | CDRRMO Head / HRMO           |\n| HR-05 | HR-F04; duty roster; exception log               | 2.10–2.11; 2.21.5        | CDRRMO Head / division leads |\n| HR-06 | HR-F05; EOC designation register                 | 2.10; 2.21.5             | CDRRMO Head / EOC Manager    |\n| HR-07 | HR-F06; restricted referral record; PPE register | 2.13; 2.21.6             | CDRRMO Head / HRMO / OSH     |\n| HR-08 | HR-F07; SPMS records; HR-F08                     | 2.14; 2.17; 2.21.7       | CDRRMO Head / HRMO           |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch2_Annex_2-W.md (Chapter 2 draft, 31 Oct 2026)','draft')
